From 90a012ee546febcc94893b01abdb4cc79679f1a6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 11:55:50 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Route generator: resolve objective positions from the vanilla
 database

124 steps across the six generated routes told the player to go and do
something without a .goto -- every no-goto warning the guide lint reported,
and all of them in generated routes. Objective positions were read from the
harvest and from ATT but never from the bundled pfQuest database, which is
the only source that knows a vanilla zone nobody has walked on the beta.

pfQuest stores objectives as references rather than coordinates, so they are
resolved rather than looked up, following quest items through to the NPCs
that drop them. One position stands for a mob with many spawns: the spawn
with the most neighbours within eight map percent, and a real spawn rather
than an average, because the average of two camps across a river is the
river.

Each source counts only if it yields a position in this zone. Chaining them
with `or` on a spots table merely existing looks equivalent and is not: a
quest the harvest saw in a neighbouring zone short-circuits the chain while a
good vanilla position sits unread. That was 31 of the 87 now fixed.

87 of 124 resolved; lint warnings 189 -> 102. route-shape.json is
deliberately not re-recorded -- the generated routes backtrack 50-66% against
the hand-written routes' 25-53%, and that gap is now visible rather than
hidden behind steps that were measured as if the walk to the objective did
not exist. Closing it means batching objectives across hubs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UByFVfcgLvVfTrfp9zrTMM
